保罗指的是这样一个事实：第一部《洛奇》电影中训练蒙太奇最著名的部分——跑上博物馆台阶和击打生肉——实际上是取自弗雷泽真实的训练日常。弗雷泽确实在2015年有了一座雕像，但对许多费城人来说，这座12英尺高的青铜塑像远未能对现实生活中的拳击传奇人物给予公平的致敬，特别是与洛奇所受到的喜爱相比。我们听说乔·弗雷泽没有得到应有的待遇，存在着一个为他的传奇做对的机会。

44
00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:48.000
His image is not emblazoned on tour buses, and the steps that he ran up are called the Rocky steps. That imbalance and the question it raised around race were soon brought into even sharper focus. In the summer of 2020, after the murder of George Floyd, the ongoing fight over America's monuments heated up once again. Ordinary citizens toppled statues depicting historical figures associated with racist ideas. Five days after Floyd was killed, someone set fire to the Rizzo statue. In Marconi Plaza, groups of mostly white residents armed with clubs and guns surrounded a Columbus statue to guard it from being torn down.
他的形象没有印在旅游巴士上，而他跑过的台阶却被称为洛奇台阶。这种失衡以及它引发的有关种族的疑问很快被推到了更加鲜明的焦点上。在2020年夏天，在乔治·弗洛伊德被谋杀后，关于美国纪念碑的持续斗争再次白热化。普通公民推翻了描绘与种族主义思想相关的历史人物的雕像。弗洛伊德被杀五天后，有人放火烧了里佐雕像。在马可尼广场，主要由手持棍棒和枪支的白人居民组成的群体包围了一座哥伦布雕像，以防其被拆除。

45
00:26:48.000 --> 00:27:14.000
As for Rocky, now that his statue was considered a monument, it would have to face the same scrutiny as these other statues. Here was a tribute to a fictional white movie character who many felt had stolen the spotlight from a real hometown black boxing champion. Surely that meant Rocky's days were numbered. But that's not how things played out. Philly's largest Black Lives Matter demonstrations kicked off every day.
至于洛奇，既然他的雕像被认为是一座纪念碑，它就必须面对与这些其他雕像相同的审视。这里是对一个虚构的白人电影角色的致敬，许多人认为他抢走了现实生活中黑人拳击冠军的风头。这当然意味着洛奇的日子不多了。但事情的发展并非如此。费城最大的“黑人的命也是命”示威活动每天都在

46
00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:46.000
day at the art museum steps. Thousands of protesters gathered right next to the Rocky statue. And instead of being torn down or moved somewhere else, Rocky was incorporated into the rallies. So like, where's Rocky in all of this? Someone has put a sign on Rocky that reads, no justice, no peace. Not only did Rocky get a role in the Black Lives Matter protests, but people started using him for other causes, putting all sorts of stuff. on his bronze body.
艺术博物馆台阶上拉开帷幕。成千上万的抗议者聚集在洛奇雕像旁边。洛奇不仅没有被拆除或搬到别处，反而被纳入了集会之中。那么，洛奇在这其中扮演什么角色呢？有人在洛奇身上挂了一个标语，上面写着：没有正义，就没有和平。洛奇不仅在“黑人的命也是命”抗议活动中扮演了角色，人们还开始将他用于其他事业，在他的青铜机体上挂上各种各样的东西。

47
00:27:46.000 --> 00:28:01.000
You have a face mask in the early days of the lockdown. You have a Ukrainian flag. When the Eagles' famed defensive end, Brandon Graham, retires, he puts his cleats on Rocky. Rocky became this container for the city's complicated
在封锁的早期，你有一个口罩。你有一面乌克兰国旗。当老鹰队的著名防守端锋布兰登·格雷厄姆退役时，他把自己的球鞋挂在了洛奇身上。洛奇成了这座城市复杂且

48
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:19.000
and sometimes contradictory emotions. Paul saw this on a day early in the pandemic when he looked at the line of people waiting to take pictures with the statue. So there's a black family and as they're posing for a photo, everyone holds up the black power fist of solidarity.
有时相互矛盾的情绪的容器。保罗在疫情初期的一天看到了这一幕，当时他看着排队等待与雕像合影的人群。所以有一个黑人家庭，当他们摆姿势拍照时，每个人都高举着声援的黑人力量拳头。

49
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:36.000
And three or four people later, there's like a group of white guys, I think they were in their early 20s, hold up a white power sign. So these two things are happening almost together, but not confrontationally? Yeah, that's right. The rocky statue could hold all of this.
三四个人之后，有一群白人小伙子，我想他们大概二十岁出头，举起了一个白人至上主义的手势。所以这两件事几乎是一起发生，但不是对抗性的？是的，没错。洛奇雕像能够承载所有这一切。

50
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:56.000
Whether you liked it or hated it, thought it was beautiful or ugly, agreed with the person next to you in line, or found their views apporrent, The statue had become linked to the whole city. It was like a song everyone in Philly knew, and people could remix it in lots of ways so that it meant something just for them.
无论你喜欢它还是讨厌它，认为它是美的还是丑的，同意排在你旁边的人的观点，还是觉得他们的观点令人反感，这座雕像已经与整座城市联系在了一起。这就像费城每个人都知道的一首歌，人们可以用很多方式对其进行重新混音，使其对他们自己具有特殊的意义。

51
00:28:56.000 --> 00:29:18.000
In 2020, the Frank Rizzo statue got moved into storage. The Columbus statue had a plywood box placed over it while the city decided what to do with it. But Rocky? His statue has only gotten more popular. Paul Farber guests curated a show about box. at the Philadelphia Museum of Art. And what did the exhibition feature?
2020年，弗兰克·里佐雕像被移入仓库。哥伦布雕像则被罩上了一个胶合板箱，而市政府则在决定拿它怎么办。但是洛奇呢？他的雕像只变得更受欢迎了。保罗·法伯曾担任费城艺术博物馆一个关于拳击的展览的客座策展人。展览展出了什么？

52
00:29:18.000 --> 00:30:02.000
None other than the statue that had been repeatedly kicked off its steps. Paul had moved it from the bottom of the steps to inside the museum for the show. Once that was over, Rocky moved again back outside. And this time, it was right where Stallone had always wanted it at the top of the museum steps, permanently, at least for now. Read the Philly Inquirer any week, and you'll see there's still deep disagreement about whether this is the right place for it. Some people think the statue has found its rightful home. Others hate that it clogs up the museum plaza, with vendors selling Rocky-related chotchkes. And others are just tired of talking about it.
正是这座曾多次被赶下台阶的雕像。保罗为了这个展览，将其从台阶底部移到了博物馆内部。展览结束后，洛奇又被搬回了室外。这一次，它正好位于史泰龙一直希望它在的地方——博物馆台阶的顶端，永久地，至少目前是这样。每周随便翻看《费城问询报》，你都会发现，对于这是否是它的正确位置，仍然存在着深刻的分歧。有些人认为这座雕像找到了它应有的家。另一些人则讨厌它堵塞了博物馆广场，还有小贩在兜售与洛奇相关的廉价纪念品。还有人只是厌倦了谈论它。

53
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:44.000
In an additional move that some see as a tribute and others as a consolation prize, Joe Fraser's statue has been moved to Rocky's old spot. at the bottom of the museum steps and a little to the side. When this started, there was a sense that it was Rocky fighting to get to the top of the museum steps. And there were people against that. So, like, did Rocky win? I don't think that there is a simple winner. Let the never-ending Rocky series show us that what we're seeing right now is just another chapter in a story that will keep unfolding.
在另一个被一些人视为致敬、被另一些人视为安慰奖的举动中，乔·弗雷泽的雕像被移到了洛奇以前的位置——艺术博物馆台阶的底部并稍微偏侧一点。这一切刚开始时，有一种感觉，那是洛奇在争取登上博物馆台阶的顶端。并且有人反对这一点。那么，就像，洛奇赢了吗？我不认为有一个简单的赢家。永无止境的《洛奇》系列向我们表明，我们现在看到的只是一个将继续展开的故事的又一个章节。

54
00:30:44.000 --> 00:31:07.000
Monuments are not conclusions. They're not periods at the end of a sentence. Nothing is forever. No monument is permanent. Every champion throws a last punch. Even Rocky had to hang up his gloves eventually. It's true. Nothing in this world lasts forever.
纪念碑不是结论。它们不是句号。没有什么东西是永远的。没有一座纪念碑是永久的。每个拳击冠军都会打出最后一拳。甚至连洛奇最终也必须挂起他的手套。确实如此。这世上没有什么东西是永恒的。

55
